# Canonicalisation redirects, so the variant URL forms return 308 rather than the 307 that
# `html_handling: "drop-trailing-slash"` emits. 307 is a TEMPORARY redirect: it tells a
# crawler the move might be undone, which is the wrong signal for a permanent
# canonicalisation. See issue #1494.
#
# EXPERIMENT — this is the whole question the issue asks: Cloudflare documents _redirects
# for Workers static assets with 301/302/303/307/308 support and says "redirects execute
# before headers", but says nothing about whether they run before html_handling. If
# html_handling wins, these rules are dead and the file goes away again.
#
# `*` is a splat matching the rest of the path, `:splat` substitutes it. Two dynamic rules
# out of the documented 100.
#
# Watch for a redirect loop on `/`: the second rule needs `/<something>/`, so `/` should
# not match — but "should not" is why this is tested on a preview and not on production.
/*.html /:splat 308
/*/ /:splat 308
